commentBody:
@john ezra
For me (on an Android phone, no app) it appears as a yellow/orange highlight box around the (already yellow) selected square. Very annoying because it obscures the letter entered in the box above.

PROTIP!: I found I can make it disappear by tapping any white space surrounding the puzzle grid. I have to this every time, but it's a good temporary workaround until the bugfeature is eventually 86ed.

@aslev

Congratulations!  Don't believe the people who downplay streaks.  They are fun to achieve and maintain, and they reward consistency and discipline.  

Doing the crossword together with your mom also sounds really fun.  (Mine taught me how to cook, appreciate books, treat pets as family, and treat people nicer than they deserved, but crosswording was not her thing!)

@aslev,
Wow -- congratulations!! I'm closing in on my 500th, but can't imagine being able to double it!! 
Well done to you & your mom!👏🏼🏆🏆👏🏼

@B
Thank you for not including an emoji.
Ha, ha.

@SP

We agree again!

"Proszę?" ("Please?") means "Could you repeat that" in Polish, too, but I've always found it an awkward way of expressing the sentiment, so I never use it myself.

@SP
and did she stick spoons in flower pots to re-kosher them? A couple of our Jewish friends had grandparents who did that. 
