Blame it on the Rathbone. And (don't laugh!) for some reason, open vowels are classier than tight or long flat vowels. It's mah-dam, not ma-dam; rah-ther, not ra-ther; bah-zəl, not bei-zəl. 
Remember the elocution coach in Singin' in the Rain coaching the extremely irritating actress to say "I cahn't stahnd it" and her repeating it as "I cain't stain' it".

