@Petrol

I think trying to communicate in Polish while not actually knowing it is generally a problem, not only while renting a car? 

Very few initialisms are used outside professional jargon (there they are endemic, and I phi-ing hate it). Also, while they appear more often in writing, they are very rarely actually spoken. Take KM (koń mechaniczny, horse power; as opposed to km, kilometer, or kilometr in Polish) - we write it down as KM but when talking we always say "konie mechaniczne".

